# P2P group owner forced to 5 GHz, laptop as a legacy station, 2026-11-27.
# Curated transcript. Passphrases are redacted. USB adb was the lifeline; the
# phone hotspot and every STA were off, so the group was the only link.

# 1. Create the group with a config, not the no-arg overload. The builder
#    requires an SSID and passphrase when no peer is given; the frequency is a
#    hint to the HAL ("peer address must be set if network name and passphrase
#    are not set" is what a bare frequency throws).
$ adb shell am start -n org.phonelink.p2pprobe/.MainActivity \
      --ei freq 5180 --es ssid DIRECT-KL-5G --es psk <redacted> --ei hold 240000
11-27 20:37:03.345  P2PSelfTest: createGroup on 5180 MHz, ssid DIRECT-KL-5G
11-27 20:37:03.360  P2PSelfTest: createGroup: success
11-27 20:37:04.864  P2PSelfTest: group owner: true
11-27 20:37:04.865  P2PSelfTest: group ssid: DIRECT-KL-5G
11-27 20:37:04.865  P2PSelfTest: group passphrase: <redacted>
11-27 20:37:04.865  P2PSelfTest: group interface: p2p-p2p0-0
11-27 20:37:04.868  P2PSelfTest: holding the group for 240000 ms

$ dumpsys wifip2p | grep "CURRENTLY OPEN"
netId=-1, startTime=11-27 20:37:03.399, channelFrequency=5180, groupRole=GroupOwner, numConnectedClients=0, ... CURRENTLY OPEN EVENT
$ ip -4 -o addr show p2p-p2p0-0
44: p2p-p2p0-0    inet 192.168.49.1/24 brd 192.168.49.255 scope global p2p-p2p0-0

# 2. The laptop's 8265 sees the group on channel 36 and joins it as a plain
#    WPA2 station. The phone's DHCP hands out 192.168.49.149.
$ nmcli -f SSID,BSSID,CHAN,FREQ,SIGNAL device wifi list | grep DIRECT
DIRECT-KL-5G         92:45:FE:DB:CF:F8  36    5180 MHz  100
$ nmcli device wifi connect DIRECT-KL-5G password <redacted> ifname wlp110s0
Device 'wlp110s0' successfully activated
$ ip -4 -o addr show wlp110s0
2: wlp110s0    inet 192.168.49.149/24 brd 192.168.49.255 scope global dynamic noprefixroute wlp110s0
$ dumpsys wifip2p | grep "CURRENTLY OPEN"        # on the phone
netId=-1, ... channelFrequency=5180, groupRole=GroupOwner, numConnectedClients=1, ... CURRENTLY OPEN EVENT

# 3. adb over the phone-hosted group: no AP, no hotspot, no cable, toggle off.
$ adb connect 192.168.49.1:5555
connected to 192.168.49.1:5555
$ adb -s 192.168.49.1:5555 shell 'id -u; getprop service.adb.tcp.port; settings get global adb_wifi_enabled'
2000
5555
0
$ ping -c2 -W2 192.168.49.1
2 packets transmitted, 2 received, 0% packet loss, time 1002ms
rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 1.806/2.478/3.150/0.672 ms

# 4. Still up 30 s later.
$ adb -s 192.168.49.1:5555 shell 'echo STILL_OK_30S'
STILL_OK_30S

# Limits measured in the same run:
# - the group lives on the probe's 240 s timer, not a foreground service, so
#   the lease dies when the hold ends;
# - the toggle still needs a STA (tests/fixtures/p2p-toggle-gate.log);
# - with the group up, a later STA association did not survive (the link broke
#   within ~3 min), so keep the two apart.
